My list items relevant:
- #1 Reckon before battle: count before commit, compare, source knowledge from people not omens/precedent/arithmetic. This maps: before accepting a change to the method, count what's compared; where the facts come from.
- #2 Make yourself unbeatable first; win then seek battle: build on what you control, not on the enemy's restraint. Maps: the design must not rely on the model choosing to read; must be loaded. This is the core of the change (delivery).
- #3 Whole over broken; strike plans first, walled cities last: prefer whole over broken; rank targets. Maps: prefer one whole copy over a second broken copy; strike the plan (the rule/design) before the code? Hmm — the "decision first, code second" analog. Also "no second copy".
- #4 Know whether you can fight; know self and other: five ways, knowing ground. Maps: do we know whether the change can work (is `project-memory/` built? SoT accepted but unbuilt)? Half a victory if the ground (the store) doesn't permit. This is the key "the pointer leads to rules with no store" issue.
- #12 Seek it in 勢 (position/conditions), not in people: change the conditions, not exhort the people. Maps exactly: don't rely on the agent's virtue/goodwill to read memory; set the position (harness/manifest). The COO's change follows this.
- #5 Move only on advantage, never from anger: don't move without advantage. Maps: don't add structure without advantage; each addition needs a reason. 老子's subtraction and "no new sentence without a report id or run."
- #6 Mix harm into benefit: state the price. Maps: each recommendation names cost.
- #8 Value victory not duration; speed: use what's ready, don't prolong. Maps: the interim while SoT is unbuilt — the pointer points to nothing; maybe keep something actionable.
- #11 Foreknowledge from people, pay: facts must come from sources. Maps: the change cites finding ids; labels.
- #16 Orders clear first, then enforced: if orders unclear it's the general's fault. Maps: the method's instruction must be clear and checkable; the denial clause.
- #18 Meet their state: avoid keen spirit, strike when flags. Maybe not needed.
